# Third-party notice and derivative-work summary

EADLD (End-to-End Auto Diffractive Lens Design) is derived from the
EISOPTX / Generalized Aberrations project:

- Project page: https://light.princeton.edu/generalized-aberrations
- Original license: MIT
- Original copyright notice: Copyright (c) 2026 princeton-computational-imaging

The original MIT license text is preserved in `LICENSE`.

This derivative adds and validates, among other project-specific changes:

- piecewise annular refractive-surface geometry and differentiable intersection;
- harmonic annular topology generation with fixed zone boundaries;
- integer-OPD branch constraints and coherent wavefront residuals;
- Levenberg–Marquardt workflows for continuous annular refinement;
- optical-path accumulation and direct scalar Kirchhoff propagation aligned with the RayWave reference convention;
- annular singlet and multi-element configurations and regression tests.

This notice documents provenance; it does not change the terms of the MIT license.
